{:edb/db-before-t 2227 :edb/db-after-t 2228 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535540 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:08:46.478Z" 13194139535540 true] [17592186179701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354335 13194139535540 true] [17592186179702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354342 13194139535540 true] [17592186179705 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354349 13194139535540 true] [17592186179925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535540 true] [17592186179925 1100 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u+2v+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-y+1,\\,v=by-x+c,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186179925 1100 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$x = u + v, y = u + 2v + 1$.\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation $T^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n$u = ax - y + 1, v = by - x + c$,\nwhat is the value of $a + b + c$?" 13194139535540 false] [17592186179925 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u+2v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot x+1\\cdot (y-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+1 \\\\ y-x-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-y+1,\\,v=1y-x+(-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-1)=2.\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186179926 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535540 true] [17592186179926 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186179926 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nFind $a + b + c$, given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation $T^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535540 false] [17592186179926 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+1+(-8)=-9.\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354336 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1089 "q-124235" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1113 #uuid "feab6d6e-33b5-5eb2-bb1f-ab10bdc595ae" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354335 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+\\frac{3}{2}+(-\\frac{5}{2})=1.\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354337 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354338 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354339 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354340 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354341 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1041 "selection" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354337 13194139535540 true] [17592186354336 1110 #uuid "b27332fa-356d-5922-87ea-b419456c01ac" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354337 1034 "1" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354337 1111 #uuid "c7a409b5-603b-59ba-a293-2c7dc9d925c9" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354338 1034 "-3" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354338 1111 #uuid "e62df2d2-711b-5010-beb3-70ed3ba42ff2" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354339 1034 "4" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354339 1111 #uuid "b409bffb-45af-5b54-af50-89247a1a0b1c" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354340 1034 "0" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354340 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354340 1111 #uuid "504ed4e4-7836-5486-993c-4635ecb0294e" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354341 1034 "-1" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354341 1111 #uuid "b9f77a26-1543-5055-8f7c-c06ae6f3f69e" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354343 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1089 "q-124315" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1100 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=5u-9v-2,\\,y=4u-8v+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-\\frac{9}{4}y+b,\\,v=cx-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1113 #uuid "e3a5a3c5-1708-5cd7-9807-5f4074faf005" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354342 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v-2 \\\\ 4u-8v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v \\\\ 4u-8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-8\\cdot 5-(-9)\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+2 \\\\ y-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (x+2)-\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot (y-4) \\\\ 1\\cdot (x+2)+(-\\frac{5}{4})\\cdot (y-4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13 \\\\ x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13,\\,v=1x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+13+1=16.\n$$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354344 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354345 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354346 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354347 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354348 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1041 "selection" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354344 13194139535540 true] [17592186354343 1110 #uuid "3d5d03d6-13c2-5935-a0a5-45865204f063" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354344 1034 "16" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354344 1111 #uuid "6a2795aa-bf46-557e-85ff-dc8d84919010" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354345 1034 "8" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354345 1111 #uuid "ad75057a-afa1-5b92-afd8-466159757648" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354346 1034 "7" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354346 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354346 1111 #uuid "06c77987-242f-5694-9817-70165eecc4d0" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354347 1034 "2" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354347 1111 #uuid "bdea084c-4bc0-59c9-9d68-bd11ad1f47fb" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354348 1034 "6" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354348 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535540 true] [17592186354348 1111 #uuid "68acfe75-6c82-558d-bf10-5b8068628003" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354350 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1089 "q-162196" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/assets/576d60f179b56159504efc59178ada3db798046d01a7dbc92986cd1162f770ea.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=u+2v+1,\\,y=2u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the square shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1113 #uuid "f811f6dd-e70f-56f6-bb39-b296a41aff91" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354349 1145 "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v+1 \\\\ 2u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible and the image of the square under the action of $T$ is a parallelogram." 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354351 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354352 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354353 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354354 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354355 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1041 "selection" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354352 13194139535540 true] [17592186354350 1110 #uuid "8a7d3d4a-7ea2-532d-8f87-fd8bd24a8b9d" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354351 1034 "A cube" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535540 true] [17592186354351 1111 #uuid "f34976aa-fc77-51c8-a4fd-b0f855832836" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354352 1034 "A parallelogram" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535540 true] [17592186354352 1111 #uuid "960fac8e-9206-5f5d-adf9-9eff3033f8d1" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354353 1034 "A point" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535540 true] [17592186354353 1111 #uuid "452fc7ad-66ac-5f31-89c3-d118473678ed" 13194139535540 true] [17592186354354 1034 "A triangle" 13194139535540 true] 